# doc.txt

Dataset: moon-eclcraters — Lunar eclipse crater timings, 94 eclipses 1842-2011 (Herald & Sinnott,
  VizieR VI/140), reduced with DE440 into the radius and shape of the Earth's shadow
File: data/moon/eclcraters/raw/doc.txt
SHA-256: 5b9144cf4c0321a13ef2e1eb50aeabcefedfceaff025765b1888c1303839721f (also in
  data/moon/eclcraters/inputs.lock; check with: cd data/moon/eclcraters && sha256sum -c inputs.lock)
In the public repository: no, only this description and the hash: CDS/VizieR distributes it free for
  scientific use with citation; its terms do not say that a copy may be republished, so only the
  hash and the request are given. Get it from https://vizier.cfa.harvard.edu/ftp/cats/6/140/doc.txt
  (or fog fetch moon-eclcraters), then compare its SHA-256 with the one above.
Obtained: downloaded as published (fog fetch or by hand).
From: VizieR VI/140, documentation.
URL: https://vizier.cfa.harvard.edu/ftp/cats/6/140/doc.txt
Check it yourself: fog verify moon-eclcraters (tools/) downloads it again into a temporary directory
  and compares it with this hash.
Collected: 2026-10-28
Licence: other — VizieR catalogue VI/140 (CDS), free for scientific use with citation; IAU
  Gazetteer of Planetary Nomenclature (USGS), public domain; JPL DE440, public.
Sources:
- D. Herald and R. Sinnott, Catalogue of Lunar Eclipse Crater Timings, J. Brit. Astron. Assoc. 124
  (2014) 247-253; VizieR VI/140 <https://vizier.cfa.harvard.edu/ftp/cats/6/140/>
- IAU Working Group for Planetary System Nomenclature, Gazetteer of Planetary Nomenclature, Moon
  (USGS Astrogeology), feature centre points <https://planetarynames.wr.usgs.gov/>
- R. S. Park, W. M. Folkner, J. G. Williams and D. H. Boggs, The JPL Planetary and Lunar Ephemerides
  DE440 and DE441, Astron. J. 161 (2021) 105
  <https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/naif/generic_kernels/spk/planets/>
Evidence class (rule 10): measure
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): A shadow whose radius changes with the direction
  around its centre as a disc's would (its polar semi-axis |sin δ☉| of the equatorial one), or no
  shadow edge at all.
Built by: fog build moon-eclcraters
