- src/tabs/moon/formfigs.js
Shown on the page:
- #tab-moon/moon-h2ecl
- #tab-moon/moon-h2shape
Notes: The shape (σ against the latitude on the shadow, each eclipse divided by its own median)
  uses angles only: a measure. The radius R_s uses the DE440 distances and a catalogue that kept
  only timings whose layer height, computed from the Earth's radius, lies between -50 and +250 km: a
  check. Schmidt's clocks (1842-1879) were corrected by Soulsby against modern ephemerides (doc.txt
  4.5). Method and references: go doc -all ./internal/build/eclcrater.

Written by `fog build explain` from data/moon/eclcraters/dataset.json and data/moon/eclcraters/inputs.lock: edit those, not this file.
